## 3. Notes & Follow-ups

* **Why not reuse `WP_SR_CLOSED`:** `WP Closed SR Action Set` resets `WP_SR_CLOSED` right after calling `ResumeParentSRs` (still inside `WriteRecord`), so it's already empty by the time `WriteRecordUpdated` executes. It also only covers `Service Request` and `Related Service Request`, not the Thin/EAI BCs.
* **Pre-implementation check (KN-370):** Confirm with the team whether any synchronous `WriteRecord`/`PreWriteRecord` logic performs cascading SR closures (`Closed -> Closed`) in the same session, and run a smoke test in dev across `WP EAI Service Request`, one `Thin` BC, and a parent/child SR closure.
* **Scope parity (`WriteRecordNew` / EIM):** SRs inserted directly as `Closed` fire `WriteRecordNew` (not `WriteRecordUpdated`), and EIM/direct SQL bypasses BC events — both behave the same as today.
* **Data quality follow-up (separate from KN-370):** If downstream Kafka consumers rely on `STATUS_SET_DT` in the payload being populated on EAI closures, adding `On Field Update Set` to the 3 missing BCs (`WP EAI Service Request`, `WP Related Service Request EAI BC`, `WP MF Related Service Request BC`) should be logged as a separate ticket.
